Amber Player is not open source. The source code is publicly visible but remains the
sole property of the author.

1. YOU MAY
   a) View and read the source code and documentation.
   b) Install and use the program packages published by the author (e.g. .deb, .rpm,
      .AppImage, .apk) free of charge for private and professional purposes.
   c) Write your own plugins for Amber Player (sound plugins, visualizers, source plugins)
      and share them freely – see section 3.

2. YOU MAY NOT – without the author's prior written permission
   a) Copy, modify or reuse the source code in whole or in part in other programs.
   b) Build, distribute, publish or sell your own or modified versions of Amber Player.
   c) Offer Amber Player or parts of it under a different name.
   d) Sell the program packages or redistribute them with advertising.

3. EXCEPTIONS
   a) The plugin templates in examples/plugins/ and the code examples in the
      documentation (docs/) may be freely copied, modified and used for your own plugins.
   b) The TouchDeck plugin in integrations/touchdeck/ is covered by its own license
      (MIT, see integrations/touchdeck/LICENSE).
   c) Third-party libraries used by Amber Player are covered by their own licenses.

4. LIABILITY
   Amber Player is provided without any warranty. To the extent permitted by law, the
   author is not liable for any damage resulting from its use.

For requests (e.g. permission under section 2): contact Marcel1853 via GitHub.
